    pk:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-fractofusus-misrai-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg–Turing wavelength for Fractofusus misrai at 63 µm (565 Ma) (Fractofusus misrai (Ediacaran spindle rangeomorph))",
        "Schnakenberg–Turing wavelength for Fractofusus misrai at 63 µm (565 Ma) faithfully reproduces Fractofusus misrai (Ediacaran spindle rangeomorph) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-fractofusus-misrai-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-fractofusus-misrai-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-fractofusus-misrai-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-fractofusus-misrai-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-fractofusus-misrai-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Fractofusus misrai (Ediacaran spindle rangeomorph) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-fractofusus-misrai-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Fractofusus misrai (Ediacaran spindle rangeomorph)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does not claim a measured 63 µm pigment ocellus. The length is the evaluation scale.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim a second assessor. R3 is open.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim the saturated peak equals 63.3 µm. It is longer, and the shift is plotted.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Pass 2 display weights oblique vanes by the activator envelope. The vane angle is a display choice; the wavelength it carries is the model's.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg a=0.09, b=0.85, D_u=0.12, D_v=2.40, grid spacing set so analytical λ_c = 6.33e-05 m. Not the slot 1251 parameters.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Three saturated fields measure how the Fourier peak moves with D_u.",
        "reported_in_source: Gehling & Narbonne 2007 name Fractofusus misrai from Mistaken Point, mid-Ediacaran ca. 575–560 Ma.",
        "reported_in_source: Hoyal Cuthill & Conway Morris 2014: fractal, self-similar rangeomorph branching consistent with osmotrophy.",
        "reported_in_source: Mitchell et al. 2015: multigenerational stolon-like reproduction plus waterborne propagules.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952: instability at a finite critical wavenumber selects a stationary wavelength.",
        "transfer_boundary: Evaluated at 63 µm on one Mistaken Point photograph. Not transferred to Fractofusus andersoni, to the 3.275 mm module's kinetics, or to Cambrian segments." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Fractofusus misrai (Late Ediacaran (Newfoundland, 565 Ma))" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Zoophyta & Vermes (Cnidaria/Platyhelminthes)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Fractofusus" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-fractofusus-misrai-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/fractofusus_misrai_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Fractofusus misrai (Ediacaran spindle rangeomorph); environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952: instability at a finite critical wavenumber selects a stationary wavelength. | Gehling & Narbonne 2007 name Fractofusus misrai from Mistaken Point, mid-Ediacaran ca. 575–560 Ma. | Hoyal Cuthill & Conway Morris 2014: fractal, self-similar rangeomorph branching consistent with osmotrophy. | Mitchell et al. 2015: multigenerational stolon-like reproduction plus waterborne propagules.; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg a=0.09, b=0.85, D_u=0.12, D_v=2.40, grid spacing set so analytical λ_c = 6.33e-05 m. Not the slot 1251 parameters. | Pass 2 display weights oblique vanes by the activator envelope. The vane angle is a display choice; the wavelength it carries is the model's. | Three saturated fields measure how the Fourier peak moves with D_u.; transfer_boundary: Evaluated at 63 µm on one Mistaken Point photograph. Not transferred to Fractofusus andersoni, to the 3.275 mm module's kinetics, or to Cambrian segments.; does_not_claim: Does not claim a measured 63 µm pigment ocellus. The length is the evaluation scale. | Does not claim the saturated peak equals 63.3 µm. It is longer, and the shift is plotted. | Does not claim a second assessor. R3 is open.]; phenomenon_size: 66 µm (6.55e-05 m, log10=-4.184 m, tier=4_cellular_10um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 66 µm to 14.7 cm): 66 µm:fractofusus-misrai-bioelectric-polarity, 205 µm:fractofusus-misrai-vertex-packing, 3.3 mm:fractofusus-misrai-turing-wavelength, 6.6 mm:fractofusus-misrai-clock-wavefront, 1.5 cm:fractofusus-misrai-morphogen-condensation, 1.8 cm:fractofusus-misrai-elastic-buckling, 2.0 cm:fractofusus-misrai-flux-canalization, 2.9 cm:fractofusus-misrai-branching-tree" ;
